# Virtual Environment
#
# Match any naming convention, not just `venv/`. A bare `venv/` did not match
# `.venv-mason/`, which is how a local virtualenv reached this public repo --
# its console-script shebangs and activate scripts each embed the absolute
# path of the machine that built it. Whoever creates the next one will not
# name it `venv` either, so these patterns cover the dot-prefixed, suffixed
# and per-user variants rather than one blessed spelling.
venv/
venv-*/
.venv/
.venv-*/
ENV/
env/
env-*/
.env-*/
virtualenv/
# The marker file at the root of every venv, as a backstop for a name none of
# the patterns above anticipated.
pyvenv.cfg

